title: 'claude kickoff/wake hygiene: drop duplicate heartbeat Monitor + always-on minimal intro'
---
From B005 audit. Two fixes in the claude onboarding/kickoff region of ocaml/cli/c2c.ml: (1) DUPLICATE WAKE — the role onboarding preamble (c2c.ml ~9781-9783, ~9858-9860) arms a 'heartbeat 4.1m' Monitor ON TOP of the native 4.1m wake.toml; remove the redundant Monitor step for managed sessions (native wake already fires; violates 'dedupe before arming'). (2) NO-INTRO PLAIN START — plain 'c2c start claude' (no role, no --auto) can hand NO intro (c2c.ml ~9910-9932); give it a minimal always-on intro so a no-role start isn't intro-less. Bundled because both touch the same kickoff code.